  "description": "TPO T172/2002 T24 [T1 ON APP] Robinia Existing size: Height: 11 m Crown spread: 12 m (approx. 6 m radius) Requested works: 2.5???3 m crown reduction on all sides, keeping the natural shape. Finished size after works: Height: approx. 8???8.5 m Crown spread: approx. 6???7 m (3???3.5 m radius) All works carried out in accordance with BS3998:2010 Tree Work Recommendations. Justification: The tree is outgrowing its location, with the crown now extending significantly over the garden and neighbouring boundaries. A proportional reduction will reduce sail area and wind loading, lowering the risk of limb failure. The work will manage the size of the tree while keeping it healthy and structurally balanced. This level of reduction is appropriate for Robinia, which responds acceptably to moderate crown reduction but poorly to heavy pruning. The reduction will improve light levels, reduce shading, and maintain the tree safely within the available space.",
